## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`BatteryComparison`** feature view (P4 · 0275) at parity with `web/src/features/vehicles/components/BatteryComparison.tsx` — a complete 10-file decomposed bundle following the established convention.

**Parity (web → native):**
- **Data:** fleet + per-vehicle state + `useUnits` bound through the P1/S8 `BatteryComparisonSource` seam (no HTTP in the view); the web `bars` non-null filter + `bars.length === 0 → return null` decision preserved and unit-pinned as `webRendersPanel`.
- **Tier:** `batteryColor` thresholds (`>60`/`>25`) ported and asserted at the 60/25 boundaries, mapped to P1/S9 status tokens.
- **Range:** `formatDistance(rated_range)` SI converter (m→km/mi, 1 digit, locale grouping, `—` fallback) ported with en_US goldens; converts only at the render boundary.
- **States:** loading / content / empty (friendly widening of web `null`) / error+retry, plus stale + offline freshness chips — all inside an always-present `TSGlassPanel` shell. Uses the shared `Activity` glyph title via the `fleet.batteryStatus` i18n key; `view.opened` telemetry; combined VoiceOver labels; Dynamic Type + reduce-motion.

